    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Aside from getting distracted easily, do you also often feel physically restless or have trouble staying still?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, totally. It's like I have this nervous energy all the time. Honestly, since I can't play soccer like I used to—which, man, I miss it so much. We had this Sunday league team, the River Rats, and we were actually pretty decent. We made it to the finals two years ago, but then our goalie moved to Texas for some tech job, and it just fell apart. Texas is crazy hot anyway, I don't know how he deals with it. \n\nBut yeah, since I'm not running around on the pitch anymore, just sitting around the house makes me feel like I'm literally crawling out of my skin. I can't just chill on the couch. I end up just pacing from room to room, picking things up and putting them down. It drives my mom crazy when I do it in the kitchen while she's trying to cook. She makes this killer lasagna, by the way, with like three different kinds of cheese. But yeah, sitting still is... it's rough.",
