    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Did you experience similar problems with staying focused or sitting still back when you were in elementary school?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, man, yeah. Elementary school was... it was a whole thing. I remember my teachers were always moving my desk around. Like, they'd put me right up next to their desk, or in the back corner, because I was always blurting things out or talking to whoever was next to me. Which reminds me, my best friend in third grade, Tyler, he had this huge collection of those crazy bones toys. Do you remember those? They were like these little plastic alien things you'd flick at each other. We got in so much trouble for playing with them during math. Tyler's actually a plumber now, makes really good money. \n\nBut yeah, school. I was always forgetting my homework, like, leaving it on the kitchen table or just straight up losing it in my backpack. My backpack was like a black hole. And whenever we had worksheets, I'd just blast through them so I could go play, but I'd make all these stupid careless mistakes. My mom used to get so mad because she knew I knew the answers, I just wouldn't slow down. She tried color-coding my folders once, which lasted about two days before I lost the red one on the bus. That bus driver, Mr. Henderson, he was always yelling at us... wait, did I answer the question? Yeah, I've always been like this, basically.",
