    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever had periods lasting several days where you needed much less sleep than usual but still felt fully energized?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, I don't think so. I mean, my sleep is usually pretty normal, unless I'm just staying up late playing video games or something. I've been playing this new open-world game, actually, and it's insane. The map is huge, like, it takes an hour just to ride a horse from one side to the other. My buddy Dave—the one who works at the warehouse—he's been playing it too, but he always plays as a mage, which I think is kind of a cheap way to play because you just stand back and shoot fireballs. I always go for the melee builds, you know? Get right in there with a big sword. It's way more intense. \n\nBut yeah, sleep. No, I don't really have days where I don't sleep and feel totally fine. If I don't get enough sleep, I'm usually pretty draggy the next day. I'll need like three cups of coffee just to function, and even then, I'm just kind of staring at the wall. My mom's coffee maker is this ancient thing from the 90s, and it takes forever to brew, so half the time I just end up going to the gas station down the street. They have this hazelnut cream that's pretty good, but sometimes the guy working there forgets to restock it. So yeah, I definitely need my sleep.",
